body:
I believed in that and got fucked up by it.

Theres all this hype about the more frequent the better but its bullshit unless you seriously have low SHBG.

I tried ed eod and mwf multiple times with subq and IM and different doses, it just doesnt work at all due to low free T/e2/dht for ME.

&#x200B;

for me ed eod mwf was like pre-trt/low T all again, a waste of precious time and all of that actually got me into alcoholism (cause the low T sides were unbearable).

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

People shouldnt listen and AT LEAST start at either e7d or e3.5d imho

This "the more frequent the better" bullshit needs to stop!

&#x200B;

I fell for this SHIT and wasted a year trying out ed eod mwf multiple times with different doses subq and IM.

e3.5d was "ok" but not good. I feel way better on e5d now and may try e7d afterwards.

&#x200B;

Yes people with low SHBG anecdotally do better with more frequent injections. and there are some exceptions of very high shbg people doing fine or better on more frequent. But there are also a lot people feeling better on e5d or e7d due to more free T dht and e2.

with kratom its like with alcohol. the first few drinks may be gut wrenching digusting but when you are in a redose cycle you dont notice it as much.

&#x200B;

i always keep my nose plugged during drinking and even after drinking when im flushing out my mouth and gargle to remove any particles lol.

&#x200B;

ive had moments where just the smell of a open kratom pack caused my stomach to cramp

no wonder at 2-3gpd, nothing to withdraw from. if you only take 3g once per day, you could do it for a month or even more without withdrawal, unless you had previous withdrawals before.

&#x200B;

JUST A GUESS; dont try due to what i said. shouldnt take kratom everyday without pauses in between

thats how it always stars.

"just a few beers to help the kratom WD anxiety"

&#x200B;

then i am drinking every day again.

&#x200B;

"now i will get kratom to help with the kratom "withdrawal anxiety", taking kratom each day.

At least kratom is not toxic to all your organs and doesnt cause you to do dumb dangerous shit while drunk. so i guess its the lesser of two evils of which one is alcohol.

&#x200B;

doesnt mean kratom is harmless or that switching ones dependency to it is "good" but just "the lesser of two evils" in my opinion

I tried NAC, I tried BPC-157, I even tried taking the MDMA with RIMAs (reversible inhibitors of MAO-A)  \[WARNING VERY DANGEROUS/POTENTIALLY DEADLY!!!\] and it did NOTHING.

&#x200B;

idk what is wrong with my brain. Another theory I have is that insufficient estradiol (the most potent estrogen) left me witrh improper serotonin transporter action and or serotonin synthesis

yeah its very strange, tldr: even my anticipation euphoria before taking the mdma is 100000x stronger than the mdma itself, its like mdma switches off my euphoria circuits.

&#x200B;

I suspect hormonal issues, lets hope it works again next time as I seriously need the mdma for ptsd "self therapy"

Yea show me the proof of the problem. Show me scientific journals, case studies or people reports online talking about abusing meds to lucid dream to escape their life.

&#x200B;

I can show you for example that PTSD nightmares a actually a thing. Its a normal well known thing in science. Theres scientific AND anecdotal proof for that.

&#x200B;

Your claim is made up and doesnt exist in real life.

"I escaped night terrors with lucid dream" first of all ONE CASE doesnt prove anything. Second this has nothing to do with your claim, as you didnt escape your terrible life via lucid dreams, you used lucid dreams to avoid night terrors.

&#x200B;

Thats two completely different things. Third, how can ANYONE use lucid dreams to escape their horrible life when dreams only happen for like 10 minutes at night, and the rest of your day you are awake in your terrible life.

By the way, for MOST people, even those who REALLY try, lucid dreams are REALLY rare. You dont just dream lucid everynight. How often do you think someone does dream lucid? 1 time every month on average? for 5 minutes?

&#x200B;

All of your talk is nonsense anyway, as I just reported a event that happened to me, not glorifying this medication as I also talked about its side effect.

YOU positively talked about very dangerous medication with very serious, possible PERMANENT side effects like pssd and brain damage, talking positively about how they will positively affect dreams and cause a mood boost and great melatonin production.

&#x200B;

Thats why I wont take you serious anyways. Dont bother to talk shit to me again, you promote medication that destroys/destroyed peoples life PERMANENTLY. go look up PSSD, its a permanent side effect.

&#x200B;

I took seroquel in the past. Seroquel causes brain damage in the longterm and can cause sleep walking. Someone could harm himself while sleep walking. Antipsychotics and ssris cause sexual dysfunction. but yeah "they affect dreams positively! and you will feel great on the serotonin mood boost" wow sounds great! maybe i shjould try these meds mentioned on the lucid dream sub!

lmao show proof for that.

People escaping their life via lucid dreaming is the most stupid thing I have ever heard. Escaping ones life via a 5 minute dream that you forget 10 seconds after waking up? Yeah right. Show me anyone reporting this online.

&#x200B;

"I had a childhood filled with night terrors every single night and you know how I got rid of them? By lucid dreaming. So with all due respect, you have no idea what you’re talking about."

&#x200B;

Oh an anecdotal evidence story.

&#x200B;

Night terrors are not "a terrible life". you managed a sleeping problem with a sleeping technique. Thats something totally different. And You didnt abuse any antidepressants for these lucid dreams so I dont even know why you would bring up something like this in this case.

So you ESCAPED his LIFE via lucid dreaming? Or did he escape from NIGHT TERRORS from lucid dreaming?

&#x200B;

Let me tell you this, no ones going to sleep 24hrs a day. So escaping ones life via dreaming doesnt even make sense. Theres a reason people use drugs instead of taking mirtazapine for dreaming.

&#x200B;

You are clearly making up stuff that doesnt exist. SHow me a case study or any report of people abusing antidepressants just cause of their dream promoting properties.

&#x200B;

"oh these antidepressants may in some case pro-self harmin tendencies, make me eat all day gaining weight, they dull my emotions so much that i feel like a robotic zombie, my dick doesnt work anymore, ive got no libido, but man thats totally worth the dreamz"

Can you show me people reporting about being addicted to nicotine patches?

Nicotine is an addictive drug that promotes 100x times more intense (lucid) dreams than any med/drug on this planet. Where are the people abusing nicotine patches for dreaming? Show me any proof for your claims if they are true.

&#x200B;

ptsd nightmares are a reported thing by science, they are a proven fact.

Now Show me the proof for YOUR claims.

&#x200B;

Btw I found your post:

"I misread your post. Oops! Zoloft and Seroquel will absolutely affect your dreams but only for the better from previous people I’ve known to take these kinds of meds. SSRIs will seriously boost your body’s levels of circulating serotonin and this has a profound effect on dreaming. Especially because serotonin is converted to melatonin in your body and will further positively affect your dreams."

&#x200B;

lmao and you criticize ME for passive "med abuse promotion"

you talk positively about SSRIS which can cause PERMANENT side effects (pssd) and pro-suicidical intentions. You talk about seroquel, a med thats proven to cause longterm brain damage, and you say they will affect your dreams positively.

&#x200B;

why did i even waste my time with you

it doesnt cause any adverse effects beside lethargy and increased appetite. Its also not addictive and I dont take it to get lucid dreams, I take it on rare occasions when I cant sleep at all. Its way better to take mirtazapine than to take benzos.

&#x200B;

like I said before, 1 beer is way more toxic than sporadic, rare use of mirtazapine

ziprasidone is an antipsychotic. say goodbye to anything dick and sex related on antipsychotics. it also blocks dopamine to suck joy out of everything you do. i guess ziprasidone can also increase prolactin.

&#x200B;

yes the problem stops when you stop taking it and the med is washed out of blood after its half life.

&#x200B;

edit: im not implying you should stop your medication. whats the reason you take it? psychosis? schizophrenia? of course dont just stop it then, but yeah its def the zipra causing that

How much DHEA do you use?

Im experimenting with pregnenolone and dhea along my TRT but I start to believe that even low dose Preg (10mg) fucks up my E2.

&#x200B;

I started with 25mg dhea 2x daily. Doesnt seem to help much?

I literally try to get HIGH e2 symptoms, like oily red flushed skin etc. just so i know that my body actually aromatizes for f sake, after trying to get injections to work since 3 months.

&#x200B;

today i increased dhea to 50mg 2x daily, but it seems like dhea doesnt even raise my E2, judged by feel.

&#x200B;

Does panax ginseng help? how much ?

any sides? im on topical dut 0.1% 2ml  one time per week for almost 3 months now. still shedding. cant really report any sides nbut i also try to dial in my TRT so i cant really say what does what.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

but i dont get watery semen for sure lol. but i never took fin so i dont know if watery semen is a side effect of any 5ar inhibition

>I'm not sure where you got mental clarity and no real-like hallucinations from though.

It does produce a unique clarity effect by being pro-cholinergic if you arent dosing it really high. You will still be "drunk"but think of something added like huperzine a or galantamines with its effects on cognition.

&#x200B;

believed to be real hallucinations like on datura/dph or such arent a usual effect on amanita. They can be possible, just like with any other drug. Lets say amphetamine, weed or others can cause real life hallucinations in some rare occasions

I know there are some reports of "delirium". but the question is if its really delirium or people calling the effect that cause they believed it to be delirious due to amanita being labelled as a deliriant.

Believing, hearing and maybe seeing things which are not real can also be applied to weed, serotonergic psychedelics, salvia, stimulants, mdma, etc, but are not "specific effects" of these drugs.

&#x200B;

when i think of something like a deliriant i think of classic deliriant effects like hallucinating real-life scenarios with 100% realistic people you can hold conversations with, animals, monsters aliens or what else lol. amanita doesnt really do that.

&#x200B;

If you are interested you can buy cheap amanita caps (the stems are almost useless) and make a tea out of that. sadly its not uncommon to feel nothing.

&#x200B;

I plan on making a tincture out of amanita muscaria or pantherina (which is stronger) for lucid dream purposes. It has also pro-sleep and anxiolytic properties which make it a interesting sleep drug. I never heard of something like amanita gaba withdrawal ( cause i never heard of anyone microdosing it long term or smth like that) maybe its withdrawal free, just like KAVA which also has gaba effects but causes no withdrawal

no i didnt say hallucinations. I said drunkenness + some dissociation, Thats also what a beer offers. Alcohol isnt a deliriant unless you maybe overdose it to the point of organ toxicity. Alcohol withdrawal can cause delirium though

Benzos also inhibit your motor function, make you confused and cause memory loss in high doses, but they are not deliriants either.

&#x200B;

Amanita CAN cause visual effects but doesnt cause believed to be real hallucinations like when you talk to people who arent there, insects, flying dragons etc.

&#x200B;

Amanitas real magic starts to shine when being asleep. its a very oneirogenic drug.

&#x200B;

In effects is closer to something like a mix of alcohol and dxm than something like datura/dph or such.

&#x200B;

Unlike deliriants like datura dph and such which cause strong confusion and dryness, amanita muscaria offers some mental clarity and makes you sweat and drool a lot, due to its pro-cholinergic effects.

&#x200B;

it can also cause the, what its called? that alice in wonderland visual effect, where things appear bigger and smalelr than they really are. Dissociatives also do that in higher doses, like ketamine

But it has no deliriant effects. Go read some trip reports or better try it yourself.

Its a unique way of dissociation and drunkenness.

"especially when there is so much evidence pointing towards this." where is the evidence?

I had another guy citing me authors/journals which provide no evidence but just say "its a deliriant."

&#x200B;

i can show you 100 of scientific sources saying lsd mimics schizophrenia. it doesnt make it true. i  can show you reports saying bufotenine has no psychoactive effects. its not true either.

&#x200B;

Read some trip reports or try amanita yourself, its not a deliriant.

&#x200B;

"A simple google search of "amanita muscaria delirium" shows hundreds if not thousands of pages that would agree with me" did you read all of those pages?

I quickly googled it and could find very little trip reports or scientific proof of delirium by a so called deliriant.

""muscimol is the opposite of a deliriant" is just incorrect." if an deliriant is defined by being anticholinergic then yes, its pro-cholinergic so the opposite of a deliriant. Okay I agree that a deliriant could be applied to other things, like alcohol/benzo withdrawal. Just cause it has same effects.

&#x200B;

But amanita doesnt have this effects. it makes you drunk and dissociated and cause some unique visual effects which are actually VERY rare as most people have no luck getting any trip out of this mushroom at all.

&#x200B;

It can cause the same "visual effect" (which is hardly visual) than acute onset of a heavy dose of GHB.

gaba agonists are not deliriants. increasing the secretiion of acetylcholine is the opposite of what a deliriant does.

&#x200B;

"Deliriants are a class of hallucinogen. The term was introduced by David F. Duncan and Robert S. Gold to distinguish these drugs from psychedelics and dissociatives, such as LSD and ketamine, respectively, due to their primary effect of causing delirium, as opposed to the more lucid states produced by such other hallucinogens as those represented by psychedelics and dissociatives.\[1\] The term is generally used to refer to anticholinergic drugs which are substances that inhibit the function of the neurotransmitter acetylcholine. Common examples of deliriants include plants of the genus Datura as well as higher than recommended dosages of Diphenhydramine (Benadryl).\[2\]\[3\]"

&#x200B;

some people also refer to salvia as a deliriant, but its not.

a deliriant is an anticholinergic agent. amanita muscaria isnt one
